WEBVTT

00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:01.983
The volatility moat.

00:00:02.033 --> 00:00:04.719
Strong brands survive turbulence when brand equity,

00:00:04.769 --> 00:00:08.290
reputation and crisis response all work together.

00:00:09.000 --> 00:00:11.886
KFC in the UK once ran out of chicken.

00:00:11.936 --> 00:00:15.686
Customers turned up to closed doors, and they were furious.

00:00:16.400 --> 00:00:17.423
But the brand owned it with a cheeky apology,

00:00:17.473 --> 00:00:20.866
and kept its equity and reputation.

00:00:20.916 --> 00:00:22.883
Tesla broke all three legs.

00:00:22.933 --> 00:00:25.918
VW survived on equity alone.

00:00:26.633 --> 00:00:27.845
Use it like this:

00:00:27.895 --> 00:00:30.663
test a brand on all three legs before a crisis hits,

00:00:30.713 --> 00:00:32.471
not after.
